-- The recursive-group hint names the member that produced the refused use's value
-- from the program alone (checker-v2.md §10.7, §10.8), so it is the
-- same in every declaration order. `hh "s"` is refused: `hh`'s body calls
-- `mb`, a member of the recursive group `ma`/`mb`/`mc`, so `hh` is
-- monomorphic. The hint names `mb`, the member `hh` calls. Reading which
-- lowered item met the mismatch would name `ma` in the orders that write
-- `ma` before `mb` before `mc` (this one) and `mb` in the others, since
-- which items are group-level then depends on the order. The hint is
-- read from the refused call's
-- callee, and written when the class is final.
type K
    = K Int


pub ma (K n) x =
    _ = (K n).mc x
    (K n).mb x


pub mb (K n) x = (K n).ma x


pub mc (K n) x =
    hh z = ( z, (K 0).mb z )
    ( ha, hb ) = ( hh 1, hh "s" )
    x
